ess","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"d21d946a0e6e007ffa601f670d96477672bb34c3211b80d70b350c7ef9ea89c7"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":125394,"output_tokens":3309,"requests":8}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"6b31acb7a0e3089d24269d30d7e88addc276a7f7f9526d7f732cd78577af4ba0"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T5c","usage":{"input_tokens":16664,"output_tokens":724,"requests":2}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"a4d849e412a3f627af4f56927dc1feb924fb088afe08bda3172ece835ba9ea80"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T3","usage":{"input_tokens":65428,"output_tokens":1708,"requests":4}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"6ab5869399733c38b9ec2c442fbbc95ce778bbf94ebe1a930b22cbf4512c6c94"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":225977,"output_tokens":4337,"requests":10}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"6275e10e8c292417cbc8c0be3156fd370241c7acff8f1185d179a3e2e524940b"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":414141,"output_tokens":7313,"requests":15}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"90cbdc1759c42ecf1d9392e56c183c36cd1659f3938e45e1af5dcf37f72747db"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":160343,"output_tokens":4160,"requests":7}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"68b716162b6b4abe375a59beb1356e74d565f45f5836de17b7e88d94d0fd9f0e"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T8","usage":{"input_tokens":351933,"output_tokens":6686,"requests":11}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the completion_read_basis receipt digest (which captures comment/evidence-set drift) a MANDATORY component of the recorded fingerprint whenever a run pinned a receipt, and specify the fallback identity + how a reader distinguishes a comment-blind fingerprint (no receipt) from a full composite — the plan-review material_fingerprint alone does not cover comments/evidence and cannot solve the named attribution gap.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["material_diff.material_basis (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py:134-153) hashes only {ticket_id, description, file_impact, children, file_impact_scope} — no comments, no evidence set","completion.py:186 attaches completion_read_basis whose receipt (ticket_view.receipt, src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py:403-436) carries tickets_oid + exact + fields — the component that changes when comments/evidence change","Problem: 'verifier inputs include ticket comments and prefetched evidence, which change without a code commit'","Plan AC1 mapping: '...and, when present, the pinned completion_read_basis receipt digest' — 'when present' makes the load-bearing component optional"],"finding":"AC1 makes the completion_read_basis receipt digest a conditional ('when present') addition to the plan-review material_fingerprint, but the plan-review fingerprint's basis excludes ticket comments and the evidence set — the exact inputs whose no-commit drift the problem statement says makes FAIL->PASS unattributable. The receipt digest is the only component that captures that drift, so an implementer could satisfy AC1 with the comment-blind fingerprint alone and NOT solve the named problem.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc6015ab102ac3a0f","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1 / Fix plan 'Acceptance criteria mapping' AC1","norm_id":"nee980ca6fa6e1219","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Local/unattested verify-completion where verified_at_sha is None and no ticket_view/receipt is pinned: fingerprint falls back to the comment-blind plan-review fingerprint, so a FAIL->PASS after a comment edit still shows an identical fingerprint and remains unattributable"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reword AC1 so the fingerprint is a composite that REQUIRES the receipt digest when a completion_read_basis was pinned (the attested/close path always pins one via completion.py:186), and record a distinct marker/era when only the comment-blind plan-review fingerprint is available, so a reader never mistakes a comment-blind fingerprint for a full input identity.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py (_compose_prepared_bundle, which calls completion_sidecar.build_payload directly at :215 on the atomic-close PASS path) to the affected-file inventory, and state where the version/fingerprint enrichment lives (build_payload vs emit) so this third PASS-emit site is covered consistently with the AC4 test.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.22,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Scope enumerates only 'src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py' and 'src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py' as emitter callers, plus the two emitter modules and a test.","src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py:215: 'payload = completion_sidecar.build_payload(result, material=material)' — a third, structural production call site of the changed function on the atomic-close PASS path, not present in the plan inventory.","AC2/scope: 'stamp the completion-verifier prompt version/content hash' inside PASS/FAIL payload construction (build_payload), which is the same function completion_bundle.py invokes."],"finding":"The plan changes completion_sidecar.build_payload but its emit-callsite inventory omits a third production caller: _compose_prepared_bundle in src/rebar/_commands/completion_bundle.py:215 calls completion_sidecar.build_payload(result, material=material) directly (the atomic-close PASS certification path), bypassing completion_sidecar.emit. AC2's unconditional prompt-version stamp added inside build_payload affects the PASS payload emitted on this path too, yet it is absent from the plan's 'Scope / file impact' and 'File impact' lists (which name only close_precheck.py and transition_close.py as emit sites).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f830b5f52e8070d8b","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan → Scope / file impact (list of touched files); File impact section","norm_id":"n684930c36ece7ba8","priority":0.68,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["completion_bundle.py _compose_prepared_bundle emits an atomic-close PASS COMPLETION_VERDICT via build_payload that silently gains the new version field with no test/behavioral acknowledgement — or, if the enrichment is placed in emit() rather than build_payload, this PASS path stays unversioned while the close-precheck PASS path gets versioned, splitting the 'PASS carries version' invariant AC4 asserts.","The regression test (AC4) exercises only the emit() path, leaving the atomic-close PASS emit through build_payload unverified for the version field."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Run find_referencing_symbols on completion_sidecar.build_payload; note completion_bundle.py:215 as a third PASS-emit caller, place the unconditional version stamp inside build_payload so all three emitters are uniform, and extend the AC4 regression to assert the atomic-close PASS payload carries the version too.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Specify the fallback when best-effort material identity or prompt version is uncomputable (current_material_fingerprint returns None, ERROR-path with no result material, local/unattested mode): define whether the sidecar omits the field, records an explicit unknown-era sentinel, and reconcile that with AC4's 'non-null' requirement (scope AC4's non-null assertion to the attested/normal-verdict path).","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.231,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC4: 'a FAIL sidecar carries a non-null fingerprint and version'","AC1 mapping: 'ERROR sidecars ... will best-effort compute current material identity so ERROR intervals are not unversioned/unknown when the verifier fails before a normal verdict'","relation_snapshot.py:474-486: 'Returns None for a deleted target or on any read error' and returns None when ctx is None","completion.py:184: result['material_fingerprint'] = current_material_fingerprint(...) — same nullable source","completion_sidecar.py:344 comment: 'verified_at_sha is None in local (unattested) mode'"],"finding":"AC4 requires a FAIL sidecar to carry a NON-NULL material fingerprint, but the plan's own material source is nullable: result['material_fingerprint'] is populated from current_material_fingerprint (completion.py:184), whose impl (relation_snapshot.py:464-486) returns None for a deleted target or on any read error, and verified_at_sha is None in local/unattested mode. The plan does not specify the fallback when best-effort material identity is uncomputable — most acutely on the ERROR path (gate_error_sidecar), where the verifier failed before _attach_completion_read_basis ran and no result['material_fingerprint']/completion_read_basis exists at all.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f746c1ebc1f0685a6","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC1 + AC4 / Fix plan 'Acceptance criteria mapping' (ERROR best-effort compute)","norm_id":"ncb5b2452117d99f7","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Verifier hits LLMUnavailableError before _attach_completion_read_basis runs; ERROR sidecar has no result material and current_material_fingerprint also returns None (target read error)","Local/unattested verify-completion run where material identity is legitimately None but AC4 demands non-null"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State that PASS/FAIL sidecars record material_fingerprint when the verifier already computed it (attested path) and omit it (leaving 'unknown era') when None; scope AC4 to a FAIL emitted with a computed fingerprint; for ERROR sidecars, record material/version when best-effort compute succeeds and otherwise leave the field absent (never a fabricated value).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Define the concrete serialized shape of verifier_prompt_version (e.g. a nested object {prompt_id, content_sha256} vs. a single delimited string) so the emitter and the longitudinal era-analyzer share one parse contract.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.365,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC2 mapping: 'New sidecars will carry verifier_prompt_version (completion-verifier prompt id + git-canonical content sha256) beside the fingerprint'","prompt_model.py:243-246 prompt_content_hash returns a bare hexdigest string (the sha256 component)","Problem statement: unversioned sidecars 'conflate formula eras' — the analyzer keys on this field","No plan text defines the field's serialization (string vs. dict vs. two keys)"],"finding":"verifier_prompt_version is specified as a composite ('completion-verifier prompt id + git-canonical content sha256') but the plan never fixes its serialized shape — single concatenated string, two named fields, or a nested struct. The longitudinal gate analyzer (the consumer this ticket exists to enable) must parse this field to decide 'same formula era', so its structure is a load-bearing part of the schema contract, not an incidental data shape.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc04cc1b4ed384824","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC2 / Fix plan 'Acceptance criteria mapping' (AC2)","norm_id":"n2cf75267acb11675","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Longitudinal FP analysis groups sidecars by formula era and must extract the content sha to compare across records","A future prompt-id rename vs. content-only edit must be distinguishable from the stored field"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Record verifier_prompt_version as a small object with explicit keys, e.g. {\"prompt_id\": \"completion-verifier\", \"content_sha256\": prompt_content_hash(prompt.text)}, and state that consumers key era comparison on both fields.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the ERROR-path fingerprint is a distinct, receipt-less, as-of-emit identity and specify that consumers must not compare it to PASS/FAIL composite fingerprints as if same-scheme (e.g. tag it with a scheme/era marker).","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4167,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["emit_gate_error (gate_error_sidecar.py:59-88) has only ticket_id/gate/cause/repo_root — no verifier result, no ticket_view/receipt","Plan: 'ERROR sidecars in the completion gate will best-effort compute current material identity so ERROR intervals are not unversioned' — but no receipt is available on the ERROR path","PASS/FAIL composite includes the receipt digest (completion.py:186); ERROR cannot"],"finding":"The ERROR-path enrichment computes current material identity at emit-time with no pinned completion_read_basis (the verifier failed before pinning one), producing a fingerprint that is (a) as-of-emit rather than as-of-read and (b) a different scheme (plan-review fingerprint only) from the PASS/FAIL composite — so ERROR fingerprints are not directly comparable to PASS/FAIL fingerprints, which the plan does not call out.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb629c7b7a0150b0b","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Fix plan 'Acceptance criteria mapping' AC1 (ERROR sentence) / src/rebar/llm/gate_error_sidecar.py","norm_id":"n765382e87937a478","priority":0.1833,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Longitudinal analysis comparing an ERROR interval's fingerprint to an adjacent PASS/FAIL fingerprint concludes 'same material' or 'different material' from non-comparable schemes"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile AC2: either stamp a formula-version/era identifier alongside verifier_prompt_version (matching the problem note's formula-era motivation), or explicitly narrow AC2's top-level wording to prompt-version-only with a rationale that the completion verifier has no separable 'formula' distinct from its prompt.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2 top: 'Sidecars record the verifier formula/prompt version identifier alongside the fingerprint.'","Problem note: 'Formula/prompt version stamping in the same record would make longitudinal gate analysis version-aware (pass-3 blocking formulas have changed over time...)'","Fix-plan AC2: 'New sidecars will carry verifier_prompt_version (completion-verifier prompt id + git-canonical content sha256)' — no formula identifier"],"finding":"Top-level AC2 requires stamping the 'verifier formula/prompt version identifier' and the problem note explicitly motivates formula-era versioning ('pass-3 blocking formulas have changed over time, so unversioned sidecars conflate formula eras'), but the fix-plan AC2 mapping realizes only 'verifier_prompt_version (prompt id + content sha256)' and drops the formula-version dimension.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe70cd24d030aa337","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC2 vs Fix plan 'Acceptance criteria mapping' AC2","norm_id":"n69ae850b84b2a41c","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future analysis tries to segment completion sidecars by blocking-formula era but only the prompt version was stamped, so formula-era conflation persists"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Decide whether the completion verifier's 'formula' is distinct from its prompt content hash; if so add a formula/era field, if not amend AC2 wording to 'prompt version' and note prompt-content-hash subsumes the formula era.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2857,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify the new verifier_prompt_version scheme against the existing plan_review.manifest.registry_version stamp — either reuse/extend that convention for the completion verifier's version identity or state explicitly why a prompt-content-hash is preferred (e.g., the completion verifier is prompt-driven, not registry-driven).","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan AC2: 'Sidecars record the verifier formula/prompt version identifier alongside the fingerprint' and mapping 'verifier_prompt_version (completion-verifier prompt id + git-canonical content sha256)'","Codebase prior art: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:139 def registry_version(...) — 'A short, deterministic stamp of the criteria registry the review ran against ... Bound into the manifest so a progressive drift-refresh can detect that the registry changed'; grandfathered per docs/adr/0053","The plan text nowhere mentions registry_version or explains why a distinct content-hash scheme is chosen over reusing the established stamp convention, despite AC1 explicitly committing to reuse existing plan-review machinery 'rather than inventing a new scheme'"],"finding":"AC2 introduces a new verifier_prompt_version stamp (prompt id + git-canonical content sha256) without considering the project's established gate version-stamp prior art (plan_review.manifest.registry_version), which already provides a short, deterministic, overlay-aware, ADR-0053-grandfathered version identity for the sibling plan-review gate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7b95ede942a93ec2","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria / Fix plan AC2 mapping ('verifier_prompt_version (completion-verifier prompt id + git-canonical content sha256)')","norm_id":"nc51843caa666673f","priority":0.